Bootstrap: docker
From: python:3.12-slim

%files
    pyproject.toml /opt/soba_matchups/pyproject.toml
    README.md /opt/soba_matchups/README.md
    LICENSE /opt/soba_matchups/LICENSE
    src /opt/soba_matchups/src
    examples /opt/soba_matchups/examples

%post
    set -eu
    python -m pip install --no-cache-dir /opt/soba_matchups
    python -m pip check

%environment
    export PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1
    export PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1

%runscript
    exec soba_matchups "$@"

%test
    set -eu
    python -c 'import soba_matchups.pipeline'
    soba_matchups --help

%labels
    org.soba.tool soba_matchups
    org.soba.source https://github.com/umr-lops/soba_matchups

%help
    Build from the repository root (internet access required for the Python packages):
        apptainer build soba_matchups.sif apptainer.def

    Bind the KNMI and ESA archives read-only, and the output workspace writable:
        ESA=/legacy/project/cersat/public/cache/project/mpc-sentinel1/data/esa
        apptainer run --bind "$ESA:$ESA:ro" \
            --bind /path/to/knmi/satellite/l2b:/path/to/knmi/satellite/l2b:ro \
            --bind /path/to/work:/work soba_matchups.sif run --recipe /work/hscat.toml

    Set reference_root to the KNMI path you bound, sar_archive_root to the same ESA path,
    and output_dir to a NEW directory under /work. No API, credentials or cache.
    The ESA root must contain extracted L2/WV OCN SAFEs and their measurement NCs.
    No L1 files are used. Output items/ contains one STAC JSON per matched imagette.
